  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "The finite-flat equivalence relation is recovered as the tensor square over its invariant ring, and the affine fppf quotient is proved finite locally free without Noetherian assumptions. The proof combines invariant norm polynomials, flat extension to infinite residue fields, the orbit description of invariant fibres, a semilocal basis chosen inside the image of one structure map, and a groupoid equalizer/basis diagram. This quotient-effectiveness and finite-projectivity construction is well beyond ordinary ring invariant calculations.",
